E,F,G,H,I,J

The November 5 2024 San Francisco A–O ballot was printed with the usual Elections Code §228 more-votes-prevails conflict instruction for charter amendments that amend the same Charter sections in competing ways. The City Attorney’s Impartial Analyses place the competing charter amendments on the ballot as consecutive companion pairs.

* Prop. E vs Prop. F – duelling District Attorney / criminal-justice charter amendments;
* Prop. G vs Prop. H – duelling police / oversight / staffing charter amendments;
* Prop. I vs Prop. J – duelling City Attorney charter amendments.

The ballot language for each pair provides that if both members of the pair are approved the proposition receiving the greatest number of affirmative votes prevails and the other is of no force or effect to the extent of the conflict. Each member of a pair is therefore capable of being nullified by the other member of its pair on a higher-vote basis. The nullifiable members are E, F, G, H, I and J.

